<p class="text-[11px] font-black text-brandOrange uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">KEY TAKEAWAYS</p>
<p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed text-sm mb-4 speakable">Qi certification is mandatory for any wireless charger using the Qi logo. The process takes 8-16 weeks and costs $8,000-$25,000 depending on power class. Using a pre-certified ODM platform (like WOWOHCOOL's Qi2 designs) can cut timelines to 3-4 weeks and reduce costs by 50-70%.</p>
<ul class="text-sm text-slate-700 space-y-2 list-disc pl-5">
<li><strong>Qi certification is mandatory and takes 8-16 weeks</strong>. Budget $8,000-$25,000 for full BPP certification, plus $3,000-5,000/year for membership and logo fees. EPP for 15W+ adds $5,000-10,000.</li>
<li><strong>Qi2 (MPP) certification is simpler than Qi 1.3</strong>: the Magnetic Power Profile locks coil alignment, eliminating interoperability testing that caused most Qi 1.x delays. Qi2 certification averages 6-10 weeks vs 12-16 weeks for Qi 1.3 EPP.</li>
<li><strong>Pre-certified ODM platform: the 3-4 week shortcut</strong>. Using a WPC-registered ODM reference design cuts certification time by 60-70% and cost by 50-70%, the default path for brands launching their first wireless charger.</li>
<li><strong>Factory certification support varies dramatically</strong>. Ask your supplier: (1) In-house Qi pre-compliance test setup? (2) Which ATL do you work with? (3) Show the last 3 Qi certificates completed for customers. A factory that can't answer all three is not ready for your Qi project.</li>
</ul>
