 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-6">1. What is Qi Certification for OEM Importers?</h2>
 <div class="bg-brandBlue/5 border-l-4 border-brandOrange p-5 rounded-r-xl mb-8">
<p class="text-[11px] font-black text-brandOrange uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">QUICK ANSWER</p>
<p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">Qi certification is the official WPC (Wireless Power Consortium) approval process that verifies your wireless charger meets global safety, efficiency, and interoperability standards. Without it, you cannot legally use the Qi logo on products or packaging.</p>
</div>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">Qi (pronounced "chee") is the global standard for wireless power. It uses inductive charging tech. The <a href="https://www.wirelesspowerconsortium.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brandBlue hover:text-brandOrange font-semibold">Wireless Power Consortium (WPC)</a> manages this standard. Qi cert makes sure your chargers work safely with all Qi devices worldwide. For a detailed explanation of the underlying technology, see <a href="/blog/wireless-charging-works" class="text-brandOrange hover:underline font-semibold">How Wireless Charging Works</a>.</p>

 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">The Qi standard has grown a lot since 2008. Today, it powers over <strong>one billion devices</strong> worldwide (WPC, 2026). This covers smartphones, earbuds, laptops, and car chargers.</p>

 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">Qi cert is not optional if you want the Qi logo. It's a strict process that checks safety, cross-device work, and performance. Without proper <a href="https://www.wirelesspowerconsortium.com/certification/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brandBlue hover:text-brandOrange font-semibold">Qi cert</a>, you cannot legally use the Qi logo on your products or packaging.</p>
 
