 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-6">4. Detailed Testing Requirements</h2>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">Qi testing is thorough. It covers all parts of wireless power. All tests follow the <a href="https://www.wirelesspowerconsortium.com/knowledge-base/specifications/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brandBlue hover:text-brandOrange font-semibold">latest Qi spec</a>.</p>
 <div class="mt-4 mb-6"><img src="/image/blog/power-bank/power-bank-fast-charge-detection.webp" alt="Qi2 wireless power bank fast charge detection testing with FOD verification and MPP alignment check at WPC authorized test laboratory" title="Qi2 Fast Charge Detection Test, WPC FOD MPP Certification" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="w-full max-w-3xl mx-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg"><p class="text-center text-slate-500 text-sm mt-3">Qi2 fast charge detection testing: FOD (Foreign Object Detection) calibration and MPP alignment verification, mandatory for WPC Qi2 certification, these tests account for approximately 60% of ATL lab testing time and cost</p></div>
 
 <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8">
 <table class="w-full border border-slate-200 rounded-xl">
 <thead class="bg-slate-100">
 <tr>
 <th class="text-left p-4 font-black text-slate-900 uppercase text-sm">Test Category</th>
 <th class="text-left p-4 font-black text-slate-900 uppercase text-sm">Key Requirements</th>
 <th class="text-left p-4 font-black text-slate-900 uppercase text-sm">Failure Impact</th>
 </tr>
 </thead>
 <tbody>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200">
 <td class="p-4 font-bold text-slate-900">Power Transfer Efficiency.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">Must maintain 70% efficiency at rated power levels across all operating conditions.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-red-600">Excessive heat generation, device damage, failed certification.</td>
 </tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200">
 <td class="p-4 font-bold text-slate-900">Foreign Object Detection (FOD)</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">Must detect and respond to metal objects (coins, keys) within specified time limits; varies by power class.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-red-600">Fire risk, safety hazard, product recall.</td>
 </tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200">
 <td class="p-4 font-bold text-slate-900">Temperature Control.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">Surface temperature must stay below 40°C under all charging conditions; coil temperature limits apply.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-red-600">Safety hazard, device damage, failed certification.</td>
 </tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200">
 <td class="p-4 font-bold text-slate-900">EMF Emissions.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">Must comply with ICNIRP guidelines for human exposure to electromagnetic fields.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-red-600">Regulatory violation, market access denial.</td>
 </tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200">
 <td class="p-4 font-bold text-slate-900">Interoperability Testing.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">Must work correctly with reference Qi receivers and at least three different certified transmitter devices.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-red-600">Failed certification, interoperability issues.</td>
 </tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200">
 <td class="p-4 font-bold text-slate-900">Power Class Compliance.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">Must meet all requirements specific to declared power class (BPP, EPP, MPP)</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-red-600">Certification denial, re-testing required.</td>
 </tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200">
 <td class="p-4 font-bold text-slate-900">Coil Alignment.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">Must maintain stable power transfer within specified alignment tolerances.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-red-600">Intermittent charging, user complaints.</td>
 </tr>
 </tbody>
 </table>
 </div>
 
 <div class="bg-brandOrange/10 border border-brandOrange/20 rounded-xl p-6 mb-6">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandOrange uppercase mb-2"><svg class="icon-lightbulb mr-2" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 384 512">
 <path d="M292.9 384c7.3-22.3 21.9-42.5 38.4-59.9 32.7-34.4 52.7-80.9 52.7-132.1 0-106-86-192-192-192S0 86 0 192c0 51.2 20 97.7 52.7 132.1 16.5 17.4 31.2 37.6 38.4 59.9l201.7 0zM288 432l-192 0 0 16c0 44.2 35.8 80 80 80l32 0c44.2 0 80-35.8 80-80l0-16zM184 112c-39.8 0-72 32.2-72 72 0 13.3-10.7 24-24 24s-24-10.7-24-24c0-66.3 53.7-120 120-120 13.3 0 24 10.7 24 24s-10.7 24-24 24z" fill="currentColor"/>
 </svg>Testing Tip</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Pre-compliance testing at independent labs (TÜV Rheinland Taiwan, UL Verification Services Fremont, SGS-CSTC Shenzhen) can save thousands. Do this before official WPC ATL (Authorized Test Lab) testing using the <strong>Nok9 CATS II</strong> or <strong>GRL Qi2 Test Solution</strong>, these are the two WPC-validated test platforms. Key pre-compliance checks: <strong>FOD (Foreign Object Detection) threshold calibration</strong> (must trip ≤500mW absorbed power per Qi v2.0 Section 5.3), <strong>Q-factor measurement</strong> (transmitter resonance frequency 100-205 kHz range, Q ≤ 135 at 100 kHz per Qi2 MPP spec), <strong>coil-to-coil efficiency</strong> (≥75% at 5mm gap with N52H magnets providing ≥420g pull force), and <strong>standby power consumption</strong> (<100mW per IEC 62301 ed. 2.0 at no-load). Pre-compliance testing at $1,500-3,000 vs official WPC re-testing at $3,000-8,000/per failure round. Find and fix issues early.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
 </section>

