 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-6">7. Qi2 vs Qi Certification Differences</h2>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6"><a href="https://www.wirelesspowerconsortium.com/blog/the-future-of-wireless-charging-qi2" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brandBlue hover:text-brandOrange font-semibold">Qi2</a> launched in 2023 as a big step up in wireless charging. It introduces the MPP (Magnetic Power Profile) for precise magnetic alignment. Here are the key differences between Qi (v1.x) and Qi2 to help with product planning.</p>
 
 <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-8">
 <table class="w-full border border-slate-200 rounded-xl">
 <thead class="bg-slate-100">
 <tr>
 <th class="text-left p-4 font-black text-slate-900 uppercase text-sm">Feature</th>
 <th class="text-left p-4 font-black text-slate-900 uppercase text-sm">Qi (BPP/EPP)</th>
 <th class="text-left p-4 font-black text-slate-900 uppercase text-sm">Qi2 (MPP)</th>
 </tr>
 </thead>
 <tbody>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200">
 <td class="p-4 font-bold text-slate-900">Magnetic Alignment.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">No (relies on free positioning)</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">Yes (MagSafe-compatible ring)</td>
 </tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200">
 <td class="p-4 font-bold text-slate-900">Efficiency.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">65-75% typical.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">80%+ with aligned magnets.</td>
 </tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200">
 <td class="p-4 font-bold text-slate-900">Power Output.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">Up to 15W (EPP)</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">Up to 15W baseline, extensible to 100W+.</td>
 </tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200">
 <td class="p-4 font-bold text-slate-900">Apple Support.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">iPhone 8 - iPhone 14 (7.5W)</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">iPhone 12+ full 15W (Made for iPhone)</td>
 </tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200">
 <td class="p-4 font-bold text-slate-900">Android Support.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">Samsung, Google, others (varies)</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">Growing Android support expected.</td>
 </tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200">
 <td class="p-4 font-bold text-slate-900">Testing Complexity.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">Moderate.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">Higher (includes magnetic testing)</td>
 </tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200">
 <td class="p-4 font-bold text-slate-900">Certification Cost.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">$5,000-$15,000.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">$10,000-$20,000.</td>
 </tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200">
 <td class="p-4 font-bold text-slate-900">Market Demand.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">Established, declining.</td>
 <td class="p-4 text-slate-600">Growing rapidly.</td>
 </tr>
 </tbody>
 </table>
 </div>
 
 <div class="bg-brandBlue rounded-2xl p-8 text-white mb-6">
 <h3 class="font-black uppercase mb-4">Which Standard Should You Target?</h3>
 <div class="space-y-3 text-sm">
 <p><strong class="text-brandOrange">Qi (BPP/EPP):</strong> Best for budget chargers, car mounts, furniture integration, and markets where Qi2 accessories aren't prevalent. Lower certification costs.</p>
 <p><strong class="text-brandOrange">Qi2 (MPP):</strong> Best for premium chargers targeting iPhone 12+ users, magnetic accessories (power banks, stands), and future-proofing your product line.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
 
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">Many manufacturers now pursue dual certification. They offer products that support both Qi and Qi2 for maximum market coverage. Our <a href="/products/wireless-charger/" class="text-brandBlue hover:text-brandOrange font-semibold">Qi-certified wireless chargers</a> include options in both categories.</p>
 
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">For more detailed comparisons, see our guide on <a href="/blog/qi2-vs-magsafe-guide" class="text-brandBlue hover:text-brandOrange font-semibold">Qi2 vs MagSafe</a>.</p>
 </div>
 </section>

