 <!-- FAQ -->
 <section id="faq" class="mb-16">
 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-8 text-center">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
 <div class="space-y-6 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What is Qi certification and why do OEM importers need it?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm faq-answer">Qi certification is the global wireless charging standard managed by the <strong>Wireless Power Consortium (WPC)</strong>. It verifies your product meets safety, efficiency (≥75% minimum), and interoperability standards. Without certification, you cannot legally use the Qi logo, sell on Amazon (which actively delists uncertified wireless chargers), or access major retail channels. Qi2 adds mandatory MPP magnetic alignment testing and FOD verification. As of February 2026, <strong>637 products are Qi2-certified, with 69.62% at the 25W Qi2.2 tier.</strong> Non-certified products risk CE/FCC compliance issues, the Qi logo is treated as a safety indicator by EU and US customs.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What is the difference between Qi, Qi2, and Qi2.2 certification?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm faq-answer"><strong>Qi (original):</strong> 5W, no magnetic alignment, obsolete for 2026 OEM. <strong>Qi2 (15W):</strong> MPP magnetic alignment with N52H magnets, FOD verification. <strong>Qi2.2 (25W, July 2025):</strong> doubles power, requires 30W+ USB-C PD adapter, active cooling, upgraded coil modules, thermal ICs handling 67% more heat. Backward compatible with all Qi devices. <strong>69.62% of new WPC certifications are Qi2.2</strong>, 15W Qi2 faces rapid margin compression. For 2026 OEM: Qi2 15W = minimum viable; Qi2.2 25W = recommended standard.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">How much does Qi2 certification cost for a new OEM product?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm faq-answer">Total first-year cost for one new Qi2 product: <strong>WPC membership</strong>, Small Business $5,000/year (best entry), Adopter $18,000, Regular $30,000. <strong>ATL compliance testing:</strong> $14,000-20,000. <strong>IOC interoperability:</strong> $3,000-5,000 (10+ reference devices). <strong>Encryption key issuance:</strong> $1,500-3,000 (5-6 weeks). <strong>Qi-ID registration:</strong> $750 (Small Business: $2,500, first may be waived). <strong>Total: $21,500-38,000 from scratch.</strong> Using a pre-certified ODM platform reduces costs by 50-70%, derivative certification is only $250 per product.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">How long does the Qi2 certification process take from start to finish?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm faq-answer"><strong>Total: 8-11+ weeks</strong> (assuming no design failures). Breakdown: encryption key issuance <strong>(5-6 weeks, longest gating factor</strong>, start early); ATL conformance testing (10-20 working days, ~2-4 weeks); IOC compatibility testing (1-2 weeks); WPC review (1-2 weeks). Qi2.2 lab testing: 3-5 weeks. <strong>Critical time-saver:</strong> run key issuance in parallel with prototype prep. <strong>Pre-certified ODM platform: 3-4 weeks total.</strong></p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">Can OEM buyers use a factory's pre-certified Qi2 reference design instead of certifying from scratch?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm faq-answer"><strong>Yes, fastest path for new OEM brands.</strong> A pre-certified ODM platform has passed WPC testing for the core module. You only need derivative certification (<strong>$250 vs $21,500-38,000</strong>) for cosmetic changes. Timeline: <strong>3-4 weeks vs 12-16 weeks.</strong> Always verify the factory's Qi-ID at wirelesspowerconsortium.com/products, the MPN must match your exact SKU. Never accept a "family" certificate without your specific model listed. WOWOHCOOL offers 21+ Qi2-certified ODM platforms.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">How do I verify a factory's Qi2 certification is genuine and not fake?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm faq-answer">Three steps: (1) Look up the <strong>Qi-ID at wirelesspowerconsortium.com/products</strong>, product must appear with matching model and manufacturer. (2) Verify WPC membership on the Member Directory. (3) Demand the ATL test report from an <strong>ISO 17025-accredited lab</strong> (UL, SGS, TÜV, Intertek). Red flags: PDF-only certificate with no database entry, mismatched model numbers, unknown lab reports, "self-certified" Qi2 (doesn't exist for MPP), generic certificate without your SKU. <strong>Qi2 logo is restricted to MPP-certified products only.</strong></p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What are the most common Qi certification mistakes OEM brands make?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm faq-answer">Top 5: (1) Starting certification after production, adds 8-24 weeks delay. (2) Not initiating encryption key issuance early, 5-6 week gating factor. (3) Accepting "family" certificates without exact SKU, triggers Amazon delisting. (4) Using Qi2 logo on EPP products, restricted to MPP only. (5) Not budgeting for WPC annual renewal, lapsed membership invalidates all certs. Also: Qi logo must be <strong>minimum 5mm height, molded/laser-engraved (not stickers)</strong>, on product and packaging.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">How do I source Qi2-certified wireless chargers from an OEM factory?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm faq-answer"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Decide, certify from scratch (12-16 weeks, $21,500-38,000) or pre-certified ODM (3-4 weeks, $250 derivative). <strong>Step 2:</strong> Verify WPC membership + Qi-ID at wirelesspowerconsortium.com/products. <strong>Step 3:</strong> Confirm power tier (15W Qi2 or 25W Qi2.2). <strong>Step 4:</strong> Specify branding, derivative cert covers enclosure/logo changes. <strong>Step 5:</strong> Request ATL reports and key documentation. <strong>WOWOHCOOL is a WPC member since 2013 with 21+ Qi2-certified ODM platforms, N52H magnets, GaN V, and complete certification docs included. <a href="/contact/" class="text-brandBlue hover:text-brandOrange underline">Request Qi2 certification consultation.</a></strong></p>
 </div>
 </div>
 </div>
 </section>

